  "body": "Home\nAbout us\nIndustries\nManufacturing and industrial\nArchitecture and Buildings\nServices\nScanning\nScan to BIM\nAs-Built Drafting\n3D Modeling\nBuilding analysis\nBOMA As-Built Digital Plans\nMatterport 3D Virtual Tours\nDigital Twins\nBlog\nCase studies\nContact\nGet in touch\n(514) 606-9604\nEnglish\nen\nFrançais\nfr\nSt-Denis Thompson Inc.\n3D Scan and 3D Modeling of Building Facades\nSetting the scene\nSince 1995, St-Denis Thompson has established itself as a leader in building restoration and construction in Montreal. The company has diversified its skills, moving from traditional masonry to general contracting covering all types of building work, including the complete rehabilitation of iconic buildings. Today, with over 350 employees, St-Denis Thompson stands out for its commitment to competence, collaboration and creativity.\nFor a project to restore the facades of an apartment tower, they asked pointSpace to provide a complete scan of the facades to help them manage the work.\nFor a restoration project or facade intervention, survey accuracy is essential. Clear documentation of existing conditions helps teams better understand the actual state of the building, identify the areas that require work, coordinate the different stakeholders and monitor project progress with greater reliability.\nThrough\n3D scanning\n,\n3D modeling\nand\nfacade drafting\n, pointSpace provides a practical technical foundation for\narchitects\n, engineers, contractors and project managers. The collected data helps reduce uncertainty, limit the risk of errors and support decision-making at every stage of the project.\nThis approach supports building documentation, 3D laser scanning, as-built facade documentation and\nconstruction progress documentation\nneeds, which are especially strategic for renovation, restoration and real estate management projects across Canada.\nP\nroposed solutions\nComplete digitization\nof the building's facades.\nCAD layout of facades:\nstructure, architecture and differentiation of materials.\nGains\nThis project allowed our clients to:\nRecord project repairs and progress more efficiently\nImprove information sharing among stakeholders\n\" The tool provided was useful in managing the progress of the work. A big thank you to the pointSpace team, the service was high quality, efficient and accurate. \"\n- Pierre-Luc Comptois,\nDirector of Expertises and Inspections,\nSt-Denis Thompson Inc\n.\nArticle by\nLouis Dallaire\nA graduate of ÉTS in operations and logistics engineering, Louis is passionate about the industrial world. His goal with pointSpace is to make data management and use accessible, because it's not always necessary to use complex tools to solve simple problems !\nComprehensive Building 3D Scanning & 3D Modeling\nView case study\nContact us !\nLouis Dallaire\nldallaire@pointspace.ca\n(514) 606-9604\nContact Us\nFirst name\nLast name\nEmail\nMessage\nThank you for contacting us.\nWe will get back to you as soon as possible.\nOops, there was an error sending your message.\nPlease try again later.\nShare by:",
